  "notes": "Two campaigns. jobshop-quote cad-features/dxf.ts (bet #2, reads customer uploads): 5/8 caught, 1 equivalent, 2 gaps, both caught after new tests (rotated INSERT array; slot centre). payapps billing/pricing.ts: 8/8 caught. Hunt: probed malformed numbers in DXF, ASCII and binary STL and STEP. STL already rejects non-finite vertices; STEP measures correctly with one corrupt point and flags volume-failed-check when many are corrupt; IGES falls back per field. DXF was the outlier (one real defect, patched). Guard class: the fix sits in pushEdges, which every edge-based DXF entity (LINE, ARC, LWPOLYLINE, POLYLINE, ELLIPSE, SPLINE, and the same inside INSERT blocks) passes through, so any later entity type gets the check too. Checks run: cad-features node --test 77/77 pass; biome check clean; tsc --noEmit (typescript 5.9.3) clean.",
